 Discovery"}],"impact":0.4,"actions":["Block or tarpit the scanning source; check whether it is an internal host.","Review which ports answered and close services that should not be exposed.","Raise monitoring on the scanned hosts: an attack often follows a scan."]},"BruteForce":{"title":"Credential Brute Force","description":"Repeated login attempts against FTP/SSH or similar services.","mitre":[{"tactic":"TA0006 Credential Access","technique":"T1110 Brute Force"}],"impact":0.75,"actions":["Lock or throttle the targeted accounts; block the source IP.","Check authentication logs for any successful login from the source.","Enforce MFA and key-based SSH; disable password login where possible."]},"WebAttack":{"title":"Web Application Attack","description":"SQL injection, XSS or login brute force against a web application.","mitre":[{"tactic":"TA0001 Initial Access","technique":"T1190 Exploit Public-Facing Application"}],"impact":0.8,"actions":["Inspect the web server / WAF logs for the payloads sent by the source.","Block the source and enable WAF rules for SQLi / XSS.","Check the application database for unexpected changes or data access."]},"Bot":{"title":"Botnet / Command and Control","description":"An infected host beacons to a controller for commands (e.g. Ares botnet).","mitre":[{"tactic":"TA0011 Command and Control","technique":"T1071 Application Layer Protocol"}],"impact":0.9,"actions":["Isolate the internal host: it is likely already compromised.","Block the controller address/domain at the firewall and DNS.","Run endpoint forensics on the host and look for the same beacon elsewhere."]},"Infiltration":{"title":"Network Infiltration","description":"A host inside the network, compromised via a malicious file, attacks or scans from within.","mitre":[{"tactic":"TA0002 Execution","technique":"T1204 User Execution"},{"tactic":"TA0008 Lateral Movement","technique":"T1021 Remote Services"}],"impact":1.0,"actions":["Isolate the internal host immediately and preserve it